{
  "title": "39: al-Zumar الزمر",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nتَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ مِنَ اللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَكِيْمِ‏(1)\nTANZEELU KETAABE MENAL LAAHE A’ZEEZIL HAKEEM.\nThe descent of the Book (Qur’an) is from God, the Al-Mighty, The All-Wise.\nاِنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ بِالْحَقِّ فَاعْبُدِ اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصًا لَّهُ الدِّيْنَ ؕ‏(2)\nINNAA ANZALNAA ELAYKA KETAABA BIL-HAQQE FAAA’BUDE LAAHA MUKHLESAN LLAHU DEENA.\nVerily, We have sent down unto thee the Book (Qur'an) with the truth; so worship thou God (alone), being sincere unto Him in religion\nاَلَا لِلّٰهِ الدِّيْنُ الْخَالِصُ‌ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اَوْلِيَآءَ‌ ۘ مَا نَعْبُدُهُمْ اِلَّا لِيُقَرِّبُوْنَاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ زُلْفٰى ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَحْكُمُ بَيْنَهُمْ فِىْ مَا هُمْ فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يَهْدِىْ مَنْ هُوَ كٰذِبٌ كَفَّارٌ‏(3)\nALAA LILLAAHE DEENO AL-KHAALESU WAL LAZEENA ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONEHI AAWLEEAAAA MAA NAA’BUDUHUM ILLAA LEEQARREBOONAA ELAL LAAHE ZULFAA INNAL LAAHA YAHKOMO BAYNAHUM FEE MAA HUM FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON INNAL LAAHA LAA YAHDEE MAN HOWA KAAZEBUN KAFFAARUN.\nBeware! Unto God alone is due all obedience; and those who take guardians besides Him, (say) “we worship them not save (in order) that they may make us near unto God,” verily God will judge between them about what they differ; Verily, God guideth him not who is a liar, an ingrate\nلَوْ اَرَادَ اللّٰهُ اَنْ يَّتَّخِذَ وَلَدًا لَّاصْطَفٰى مِمَّا يَخْلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُ‌ ۙ سُبْحٰنَهٗ‌ ؕ هُوَ اللّٰهُ الْوَاحِدُ الْقَهَّارُ‏(4)\nLAW ARAADA LAAHO AN YYATTAKHEZA LAAHO LLAASTAFAA MIMMAA YAKHLOQO MAA YASHAAA WALADAN HOWA LAAHO AL-WAAHEDU AL-QAHHAARU.\nHad God intended to take a son unto Himself, certainly would He select those He willeth of what He hath created, Hallowed is He! He (alone) is God, the Almighty.\nخَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ۚ يُكَوِّرُ الَّيْلَ عَلَى النَّهَارِ وَيُكَوِّرُ النَّهَارَ عَلَى الَّيْلِ وَسَخَّرَ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ‌ؕ كُلٌّ يَّجْرِىْ لِاَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى‌ؕ اَلَا هُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْغَفَّارُ‏(5)\nKHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQQE YUKAWRU LAYLA A’LAL AN-NAHAARE WAYUKAWRU NAHAARA A’LAL LAYLE SAKHKHARASH SHAMSA WAL QAMARA KULLUL YYAJREAA LE-ELAA MOSAMMAA ALAA HOWA A’ZEEZUL AL-GHAFFAARU.\nHe hath created the heavens and the earth with the truth; causeth He the night to enter the day and the day to enter the night, and subjected the sun and the moon; each one speedeth on to an assigned term; Beware! He is the All-Mighty, the Oft- Forgiving.\nخَلَقَكُمْ مِّنْ نَّفْسٍ وَّاحِدَةٍ ثُمَّ جَعَلَ مِنْهَا زَوْجَهَا وَاَنْزَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَنْعَامِ ثَمٰنِيَةَ اَزْوَاجٍ‌ ؕ يَخْلُقُكُمْ فِىْ بُطُوْنِ اُمَّهٰتِكُمْ خَلْقًا مِّنْۢ بَعْدِ خَلْقٍ فِىْ ظُلُمٰتٍ ثَلٰثٍ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمُ اللّٰهُ رَبُّكُمْ لَهُ الْمُلْكُ‌ ؕ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ ۚ فَاَ نّٰى تُصْرَفُوْنَ‏(6)\nKHALAQAKUM MIN NAFSIN WWAAHEDATIN SUMMA JA-A’LA MINHAA ZAWJAHAA WA ANZALA LAKUM MENAL AL-AANA’AAME SAMAANEETA AZWAAJINW YAKHLUQUKUM FEE BUTOONE MINHUNNA KHALQAN MIN BA’DE KHALQIN FEE ZOLOMAATIL SALAASIN ZAA LEKUMU LAAHO RABBOKUM LAHUL A’LAYNAA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA FA-ALQEEHE NNAA TUSRAFOONA.\nHe created you from a single being, then made He from it its mate, and sent down for you eight in pairs, of the cattle, He createth you in the wombs of your mothers a creation after a creation, in triple darkness; that is God your Lord, His is the kingdom; there is no god but He; How then are ye turned away?\nاِنْ تَكْفُرُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَنِىٌّ عَنْكُمْ‌ وَلَا يَرْضٰى لِعِبَادِهِ الْكُفْرَ‌ ۚ وَاِنْ تَشْكُرُوْا يَرْضَهُ لَكُمْ‌ ؕ وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِّزْرَ اُخْرٰى‌ ؕ ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ مَّرْجِعُكُمْ فَيُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(7)\nIN TAKFUROOA FA-INNAL LAAHA GHANIYYUN A’NKUM WA LAA YARZAA LE-E’BAADEHIL KUFRA WA TASHKUROOA YARZAHU LAKUM WA LAA TAZERU WAAZERATUN WWEZRA LAHU SUMMA ELAA RABBEKUM MMARJEU’UKUM FAYONABBEOKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON INNAHU A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nIf ungrateful ye be, then verily God is (Self-Sufficient) independent of you; and He liketh not ingratitude in His servants; and if ye be grateful; He liketh it in you; and no bearer of a burden shall bear the burden of another; then unto your Lord is your return, then will He inform you of what ye were doing; verily, He knoweth all what is in the breasts (hearts).\nوَاِذَا مَسَّ الْاِنْسَانَ ضُرٌّ دَعَا رَبَّهٗ مُنِيْبًا اِلَيْهِ ثُمَّ اِذَا خَوَّلَهٗ نِعْمَةً مِّنْهُ نَسِىَ مَا كَانَ يَدْعُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَجَعَلَ لِلّٰهِ اَنْدَادًا لِّيُضِلَّ عَنْ سَبِيْلِهٖ‌ ؕ قُلْ تَمَتَّعْ بِكُفْرِكَ قَلِيْلًا ‌ۖ  اِنَّكَ مِنْ اَصْحٰبِ النَّارِ‏(8)\nWA EZAA MASSAN INSAANA ZURRUN DA-A’A WAL MUNEEBAN ELAYHE SUMMA EZAA KHAWLAH NEA’MATAN MINHO NASEAAA MAA KAANA YAD-O’O ELAYHE MIN QABLO WA LILLAAHE ANDAADANW LLEEZELLA A’N SABEELEH QUL TAMATTAA’ BEKUFREKA QALEELAA INNAKA MIN ASHAABIL NAAR.\nAnd when toucheth man a distress he crieth unto his Lord, oft-turning unto Him; and when He bestowed upon him a favour from Him, forgetteth he that for which he did cry unto Him before, and (he) setteth up rivals unto God, that he may beguile (men) to stray away from His path; say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad! unto such a man) “Enjoy thyself in thy ingratitude a little; verily, thou art of the inmates of the (Hell) fire\nاَمَّنْ هُوَ قَانِتٌ اٰنَآءَ الَّيْلِ سَاجِدًا وَّقَآئِمًا يَّحْذَرُ الْاٰخِرَةَ وَيَرْجُوْا رَحْمَةَ رَبِّهٖ‌ؕ قُلْ هَلْ يَسْتَوِى الَّذِيْنَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ وَالَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‌ؕ اِنَّمَا يَتَذَكَّرُ اُولُوا الْاَلْبَابِ‏(9)\nAMMAN HOWA QAANETUN AAANAAA LAYLE SAAJEDAN WWAQAAEMAN YYAHZARU AAKHERATA WA YARJOO RAHMATA RABBEH QUL HAL YASTAWEAA LAZEENA YA’LAMOON WAL LAZEENA LAA YAA’LAMOONA INNAMAA YATAZAKKARU ULUL ULIL ALBAABE.\nWhat! (this or) he who is prayerful during the hours of the night, prostrating in obeisance and standing, and he taketh heed of the hereafter and hopeth he for the mercy of his Lord! Say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “What! Can those who know be equal to those who know not? Verily only the men of understanding take the warning\nقُلْ يٰعِبَادِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّقُوْا رَبَّكُمْ‌ ؕ لِلَّذِيْنَ اَحْسَنُوْا فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةٌ ‌ ؕ وَاَرْضُ اللّٰهِ وَاسِعَةٌ ‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا يُوَفَّى الصّٰبِرُوْنَ اَجْرَهُمْ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ‏(10)\nQUL YAAE’EBAADE LAZEENA AAMANUT TAQOO TAQUL LILLAZEENA AAHSANOOA FEE HAAZEHE DUNYAA HASANATUL WAARZU LAAHE WAASE-A’TUN INNAMAA YOOFFAA SAABEROON AJRAHUM BEGHAYRIL HESAAB.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “O’ my servants who believe! Fear ye (the wrath of) your Lord, for those who do good in this world (there) is good, and God’s earth is extensive; Verily, only the patient ones will be paid their recompense without any account.\nقُلْ اِنِّىْۤ اُمِرْتُ اَنْ اَعْبُدَ اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصًا لَّهُ الدِّيْنَۙ‏(11)\nQUL INNEE AN A-A’BODA AN HAAZEHIL BALDATIL LAAHA MUKHLESAN LLAHU DEENA.\nSay thou: “I have been bidden that I should worship God (alone) being sincere unto Him in religion,\nوَاُمِرْتُ لِاَنْ اَكُوْنَ اَوَّلَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ‏(12)\nWA AN A-A’BODA LE-AN SHAY-IWN WA AWWALA AKOONA MENAL MUSLEMEEN.\nAnd Commanded I am, that I shall be the first Muslim\nقُلْ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ اِنْ عَصَيْتُ رَبِّىْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيْمٍ‏(13)\nQUL INNEE AKHAAFO IN A’ASAYTU RABBEE A’ZAABAL YAWMIN A’ZEEM.\nSay: “Verily, fear I, if I disobey my Lord, the chastisement of a great day.\nقُلِ اللّٰهَ اَعْبُدُ مُخْلِصًا لَّهٗ دِيْنِىۙ‏(14)\nQOLIL LAAHA A-A’BODUL MUKHLESAN LAHU DEENEAA.\nSay: “God (It is Whom) worship I, being sincere unto Him in my religion,\nفَاعْبُدُوْا مَا شِئْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِهٖ‌ ؕ قُلْ اِنَّ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَ اَهْلِيْهِمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ ؕ اَلَا ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْخُسْرَانُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(15)\nFA BODOO MAA SHEATUM MIN DOONEHI QUL INNAL KHAASEREEN LAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM WA AHLEEHIM YAWMA QEYAAMATE ALAA ZAA LEKA HOWA AL-KHUSRAANU MOBEEN.\nWorship ye then whatsoever ye like other than Him.” Say thou: “Verily, the losers are those who have lost their own selves and their families on the Day of Judgment; Beware! that is the clear loss\nلَهُمْ مِّنْ فَوْقِهِمْ ظُلَلٌ مِّنَ النَّارِ وَمِنْ تَحْتِهِمْ ظُلَلٌ ‌ؕ ذٰ لِكَ يُخَوِّفُ اللّٰهُ بِهٖ عِبَادَهٗ‌ ؕ يٰعِبَادِ فَاتَّقُوْنِ‏(16)\nLAHUM MIN FAWQEHIM ZULALUN MENAL NAAR WA MIN TAHTEHEM ZULALUN ZAA LEKA YUKHAWFU LAAHO BEHI E’EBAADAH YAAE’EBAADE FAT-TAQOON.\nFor them shall be from above them coverings of fire and from beneath them coverings; with that maketh God His servants to fear; (so) fear Me ye O’ My servants.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اجْتَنَبُوا الطَّاغُوْتَ اَنْ يَّعْبُدُوْهَا وَاَنَابُوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ لَهُمُ الْبُشْرٰى‌ ۚ فَبَشِّرْ عِبَادِ ۙ‏(17)\nWAL LAZEENA AJTANABOOA AT-TAAGHOOTA AN YYAA’BUDOOHAA WAANAABOOA ELAL LAAHE LAHOMUL AL-BUSHRAA FABASSHER E’EBAADE.\nAnd those who shun the worship of the idols and turn they unto God, for them is the glad tidings, so bear thou the glad tidings unto My servants.\nالَّذِيْنَ يَسْتَمِعُوْنَ الْقَوْلَ فَيَتَّبِعُوْنَ اَحْسَنَهٗ‌ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ هَدٰٮهُمُ اللّٰهُ‌ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمْ اُولُوا الْاَلْبَابِ‏(18)\nLAZEENA YASTAMEU’OONA QAWLA FAYATTABEU’OONA AAHSANAH OOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA HADAAHUMU LAAHO WA OOLAAA-EKA HUM ULUL ULIL ALBAABE.\nThose who hearken unto the word and follow the best of it; those are they whom God hath guided; and those it is who are the men of understanding.\nاَفَمَنْ حَقَّ عَلَيْهِ كَلِمَةُ الْعَذَابِ ؕ اَفَاَنْتَ تُنْقِذُ مَنْ فِى النَّارِ‌ ۚ‏(19)\nAFAMAWN HAQQA A’LAYHE KALEMATU A’ZAABE AAFAANTA TUNQEZU MAN FIL NAAR.\nWhat! Is he on whom the sentence of chastisement hath been justly passed (equal to one who deserveth a reward)? Canst thou rescue him who is in the fire?\nلٰكِنِ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا رَبَّهُمْ لَهُمْ غُرَفٌ مِّنْ فَوْقِهَا غُرَفٌ مَّبْنِيَّةٌ ۙ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ؕوَعْدَ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ لَا يُخْلِفُ اللّٰهُ الْمِيْعَادَ‏(20)\nLAAKENE LAZEENA TAQAW RABBAHUM LAHUM GHURAFUN MIN FAWQEHAA GHURAFUN MMABNEETUN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO WAA’DA LAAHE LAA YUKHLEFUL LAAHO AL-MEEA’AADA.\nBut (for) those who fear the (wrath of) their Lord are lofty pavilions, above them (ever) lofty pavilions, built (for them), ’neath which flow rivers: (this is) the promise of God: Faileth not God (His) promise.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَسَلَكَهٗ يَنَابِيْعَ فِى الْاَرْضِ ثُمَّ يُخْرِجُ بِهٖ زَرْعًا مُّخْتَلِفًا اَ لْوَانُهٗ ثُمَّ يَهِيْجُ فَتَرٰٮهُ مُصْفَرًّا ثُمَّ يَجْعَلُهٗ حُطَامًا‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَذِكْرٰى لِاُولِى الْاَلْبَابِ‏(21)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FASALAKAH YANAABEEA’A FIL ARZE SUMMA KHAB-A BEHI ZARA’AN MMUKHTALEFAN A’ZAABAN LWAANUH SUMMA YAHEEJU FATARAAHU MUSFARRAL SUMMA YAJA’ALUH HOTAAMAN INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAZEKRAA LE-ULIL ULIL ALBAABE.\nSeest thou not that God sendeth down water from heaven, then causeth it go into the earth in the springs, then bringeth forth with it herbage of various colours then it withereth that thou seest it yellow, then He maketh it chaff? Verily in this is a reminder for men of understanding.\nاَفَمَنْ شَرَحَ اللّٰهُ صَدْرَهٗ لِلْاِسْلَامِ فَهُوَ عَلٰى نُوْرٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ‌ؕ فَوَيْلٌ لِّلْقٰسِيَةِ قُلُوْبُهُمْ مِّنْ ذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ‌ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(22)\nAFAMAWN SHARAHA LAAHO SADRAH LIL-AESLAAME FAHOWA A’LAA NOORIN MIN RABBEH LAHUM LLELQAASEETE QULOOBUHUM MIN ELAA LAAH OOLAAA-EKA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nWhat! is he whose breast (heart) God hath opened for Islam then he followeth the Light from God (like unto the hardhearted one)? Nay! Woe unto those whose hearts are hard against the remembrance of God; those are in a clear error.\nاَللّٰهُ نَزَّلَ اَحْسَنَ الْحَدِيْثِ كِتٰبًا مُّتَشَابِهًا مَّثَانِىَ ‌ۖ  تَقْشَعِرُّ مِنْهُ جُلُوْدُ الَّذِيْنَ يَخْشَوْنَ رَبَّهُمْ‌ۚ ثُمَّ تَلِيْنُ جُلُوْدُهُمْ وَقُلُوْبُهُمْ اِلٰى ذِكْرِ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُدَى اللّٰهِ يَهْدِىْ بِهٖ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ هَادٍ‏(23)\nALLAAHO NAZZALAL AHSANAL HAAZAL KETAABAA MMUTASHAABEHAN MMASAANEAAA TAQSHAE’ERRU MINHO JULOODU LAZEENA YAKHSHAWNA RABBAHUM SUMMA TALEENU JULOODUHUM WAQULOOBUHUM ELAA ELAA LAAHE ZAA LEKA HODAL LAAHE YAHDEE BEHI MAN YASHAAA-O WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN HAADIN.\nGod hath sent down the best recital, a Book Consistent (in its parts) with iteration, at which do shudder the skins of those who fear their Lord, then get softened their skins and their hearts unto the remembrance of God; This is God’s guidance, guideth He with it whomsoever He willeth; and whomsoever alloweth God to stray, for him there is no guide.\nاَ فَمَنْ يَّتَّقِىْ بِوَجْهِهٖ سُوْٓءَ الْعَذَابِ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ ؕ وَقِيْلَ لِلظّٰلِمِيْنَ ذُوْقُوْا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(24)\nA’ZAABAN FAMAN YYATTAQEAA BE-WAJHEHI SOOO-AL A’ZAABE YAWMA QEYAAMATE WA QEELAD LIZ-ZAALEMEENA ZOOQOO MAA KUNTUM TAKSEBOONA.\nWhat! is he then who hath to guard himself with his own face against the torment of the chastisement on the Day of Judgment (like unto him who is secure from it)? And it will be said unto the unjust: “Taste ye what ye were earning!\nكَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ فَاَتٰٮهُمُ الْعَذَابُ مِنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(25)\nKAZZABA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FA-ATAAHOMUL A’ZAABO MIN HAYSO LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nThose before them did belie (the apostles) so came there unto them the chastisement from whence they perceived not.\nفَاَذَاقَهُمُ اللّٰهُ الْخِزْىَ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا‌ ۚ وَلَعَذَابُ الْاٰخِرَةِ اَكْبَرُ‌ ۘ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(26)\nFAAZAAQAHUMU LAAHO AL-KHEZAAA FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA LA-A’ZAABUL AAKHERATE AKBARO LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON.\nThen did God make them taste the disgrace in the life of this world and certainly the chastisement of the hereafter is greater: did they but know.\nوَلَقَدْ ضَرَبْنَا لِلنَّاسِ فِىْ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ مِنْ كُلِّ مَثَلٍ لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(27)\nWA LAQAD ZARABNAA LIN-NAASE FEE HAAZAA QUR-AANE MIN KULLE MASALIN LA-A’LLAHUM YATAZAKKAROON.\nAnd indeed have We set forth for the people in this Qur’an examples of every sort that happly they may reflect.\nقُرْاٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا غَيْرَ ذِىْ عِوَجٍ لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ‏(28)\nQURAANAN A’RABIYYAL GHAYRA ZEE E’EWAJIN LA-A’LLAHUM YATTAQOON.\nAn Arabic Qur’an without any crookedness, that happly they may guard themselves (against evil).\nضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا رَّجُلًا فِيْهِ شُرَكَآءُ مُتَشٰكِسُوْنَ وَرَجُلًا سَلَمًا لِّرَجُلٍ ؕ هَلْ يَسْتَوِيٰنِ مَثَلًا ‌ؕ اَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ ‌ ۚ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(29)\nZARABA LAAHO MASALAA RRAJULAN FEEHE SHURAKAAU MUTASHAAKESOONA WARAJULAN SALAMAN LLERAJULIN HAL YASTAWEENE MASALAA AALHAMDU LILLAAHE BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nSetteth forth God the examples of the man in (the service of) associates quarrelling with each other, and of a man (devoted) wholly to a (single) man (Master). Can the two (such) ones be alike in condition? (No!) All Praise is God’s; Nay! most of them know not.\nاِنَّكَ مَيِّتٌ وَّاِنَّهُمْ مَّيِّتُوْنَ‏(30)\nINNAKA MAYTUN WWAANNAHUM MMAYTOONA.\nVerily thou shall (one day) die, and they (too) shall (one day) die.\nثُمَّ اِنَّكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ تَخْتَصِمُوْنَ‏(31)\nSUMMA INNAKUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE I’NDAL RABBEKUM TAKHTASEMOONA.\nThen verily ye on the Day of Judgment before your Lord will wrangle one with another.\nفَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنْ كَذَبَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ وَكَذَّبَ بِالصِّدْقِ اِذْ جَآءَهٗ‌ ؕ اَ لَيْسَ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ مَثْوًى لِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(32)\nFAMAN AZLAMO MIMMAN KAZABA A’LAL LAAHE WA KAZZABA BEALSSEDQE IZ JAAA-AHU A’ZAABAN LAYSA FEE JAHANNAMA MASWAL LIL-KAAFEREEN.\nWho is then more unjust than he who lieth about God and belieth the truth when it cometh unto him; Is there not in the Hell an abode for the disbelievers?\nوَالَّذِىْ جَآءَ بِالصِّدْقِ وَصَدَّقَ بِهٖۤ‌ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُتَّقُوْنَ‏(33)\nWAL LAZEE JAAA-A BEALSSEDQE WA SADDAQA BEHI OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUTTAQOON.\nAnd he who bringeth the truth and he who testifieth it - These are they that are the pious ones.\nلَهُمْ مَّا يَشَآءُوْنَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ جَزٰٓؤُ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ ۖۚ‏(34)\nLAHUM MAA YASHAAOONA I’NDAL RABBEHIM ZAA LEKA JAZAAAU MOHSENEEN.\nFor them is whatever they please with their Lord; that is the recompense of the doers of good;\nلِيُكَفِّرَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ اَسْوَاَ الَّذِىْ عَمِلُوْا وَيَجْزِيَهُمْ اَجْرَهُمْ بِاَحْسَنِ الَّذِىْ كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(35)\nLEEKAFFERA LAAHO A’NHUM ASWA-AL LAZEE A’MELOO WAYAJZEEHUM AJRAHUM BE-AHSANE LAZEE KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThat God may take away from them the worst of what they did, and recompense them with their reward for the best of what they used to do.\nاَلَيْسَ اللّٰهُ بِكَافٍ عَبْدَهٗ‌ ؕ وَيُخَوِّفُوْنَكَ بِالَّذِيْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّضْلِلِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ هَادٍ‌ ۚ‏(36)\nA-LAYSA LAAHO BEKAAFIN A’ABDAH WAYUKHAWFOONAKA BE-LAZEENA MIN DOONEHI WA MAN YYUZLELE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN HAADIN.\nIs not God sufficient for His servant? And they frighten thee with those besides Him, and whomsoever God alloweth to stray, for him there shall not be any guide.\nوَمَنْ يَّهْدِ اللّٰهُ فَمَا لَهٗ مِنْ مُّضِلٍّ‌ ؕ اَ لَيْسَ اللّٰهُ بِعَزِيْزٍ ذِى انتِقَامٍ‏(37)\nWA MAN YYAHDE LAAHO FAMAA LAHU MIN MMUZELLIN A’ZAABAN LAYSA LAAHO BEA’AZEEZIN ZIL ANTEQAAMIN.\nAnd whomsoever God guideth, then him none shall beguile; Is not God the Almighty Lord of Retribution?\nوَلَئِنْ سَاَ لْتَهُمْ مَّنْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اللّٰهُ‌ ؕ قُلْ اَفَرَءَيْتُمْ مَّا تَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ اَرَادَنِىَ اللّٰهُ بِضُرٍّ هَلْ هُنَّ كٰشِفٰتُ ضُرِّهٖۤ اَوْ اَرَادَنِىْ بِرَحْمَةٍ هَلْ هُنَّ مُمْسِكٰتُ رَحْمَتِهٖ‌ ؕ قُلْ حَسْبِىَ اللّٰهُ‌ ؕ عَلَيْهِ يَتَوَكَّلُ الْمُتَوَكِّلُوْنَ‏(38)\nWA LAIN HAQ LTAHUM MAN KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA LAYAQOOLUNNAL LAAHO QUL AFA-RA-AYTUM MAA TADU’OONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE IN AARAADANEAAA LAAHO BEZURRIN HAL HUNNA KAASHEFAATU ZURREH AW AARAADANEAA BERAHMATIN HAL HUNNA MUMSEKAATU FEE QUL HASBEAAA LAAHO A’LAYHE YATAWAKKALU AL-MUTAWAKKELOONA.\nAnd if thou ask them who created the heavens and the earth? They would certainly say: ‘God’; Say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “Bethink ye then of what ye call upon besides than God, if willeth God unto me a harm, could they be the removers of His harm, or if willeth (God) unto me His mercy, could they be the withholders of His mercy?” Say thou: “Sufficeth me God! On Him (alone) do rely the reliants.\nقُلْ يٰقَوْمِ اعْمَلُوْا عَلٰى مَكَانَتِكُمْ اِنِّىْ عَامِلٌ‌ۚ فَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(39)\nQUL LE-QAWMEHI AA’MALOOA A’LAA MAKAANATEKUM INNEE A’AAMELUN FA-SAWFA TA’LAMOON.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “O’ my people! Act ye (as ye like) in your place, verily I (too) do act, soon will ye come to know,\nمَنْ يَّاْتِيْهِ عَذَابٌ يُّخْزِيْهِ وَيَحِلُّ عَلَيْهِ عَذَابٌ مُّقِيْمٌ‏(40)\nMAN YYAATEEHE A’ZAABUN YYUKHZEEHE WA YAHILLO A’LAYHE A’ZAABUN MMUQEEMUN.\nWho it is unto whom cometh a chastisement which will disgrace him, and whom there falleth the everlasting doom.\nاِنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ لِلنَّاسِ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ۚ فَمَنِ اهْتَدٰى فَلِنَفْسِهٖ‌ ۚ وَمَنْ ضَلَّ فَاِنَّمَا يَضِلُّ عَلَيْهَا‌ ۚ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِوَكِيْلٍ‏(41)\nINNAA ANZALNAA A’LAYKA KETAABA LIN-NAASE BIL-HAQQE FAMANE’ TADAA FALENAFSEH WA MAN ZALLA FA-INNAMAA YAZELLU A’LAYHAA WA MAA ANTA A’LAYHIM BEWAKEELIN.\nVerily We sent down on thee the Book (Qur'an) for the sake of the people, with the truth; and whosoever is guided aright, it is for his own self, and whosoever goeth astray, strayeth he only to its own hurt, and thou art not over them a custodian.\nاَللّٰهُ يَتَوَفَّى الْاَنْفُسَ حِيْنَ مَوْتِهَا وَالَّتِىْ لَمْ تَمُتْ فِىْ مَنَامِهَا‌ ۚ فَيُمْسِكُ الَّتِىْ قَضٰى عَلَيْهَا الْمَوْتَ وَ يُرْسِلُ الْاُخْرٰٓى اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰیٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(42)\nALLAAHO YATAWAFFAA AL-AANFUSA HEENA MAWTEHAA WA LATEE LAM TAMUT FEE MANAAMEHAA FAYUMSEKU LATEE QAZAA A’LAYHAA MAWTA WA YURSELUR AL-AUKHRAAA ELAA ELAA AJALIM INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LAATIN LEQAWMINY YATAFAKKAROON.\nGod taketh the souls at death, and those that die not (He taketh) during their sleep; and He withholdeth those on whom He hath passed the decree of death (from returning unto their bodies); but sendeth He the others (to their bodies) till a time which is fixed; Verily, in this are signs for a people who reflect.\nاَمِ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ شُفَعَآءَ‌ ؕ قُلْ اَوَلَوْ كَانُوْا لَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(43)\nAMIL ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONIL LAAHE SHUFAA’AAA QUL LAW KAANOO LAA YAMLEKOONA SHAY-ANW WA LAA YA’QELOON.\nOr, have they taken intercessors other than God? Say thou: “What! even though they have no power over anything, nor do they understand.\nقُلْ لِّلَّهِ الشَّفَاعَةُ جَمِيْعًا‌ ؕ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ ؕ ثُمَّ اِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(44)\nQUL LILLAAH ASH-SHAFAAA’ATU JAMEE-A’A LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE SUMMA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “God’s (alone) is intercession altogether; His is the kingdom of the heavens and the earth; then unto Him (only) ye shall all be returned.\nوَاِذَا ذُكِرَ اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهُ اشْمَاَزَّتْ قُلُوْبُ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ‌ ۚ وَاِذَا ذُكِرَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اِذَا هُمْ يَسْتَبْشِرُوْنَ‏(45)\nWA EZAA ZUKERA LAAHO WAHDAHU ASHMAAZZAT QULOOBU LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE WA EZAA ZUKERA LAZEENA MIN DOONEHI EZAA HUM YASTABSHEROON.\nWhen God alone is mentioned, shrink the hearts of those who believe not in the hereafter; and when those besides Him are mentioned, lo! they rejoice.\nقُلِ اللّٰهُمَّ فَاطِرَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ عٰلِمَ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ اَنْتَ تَحْكُمُ بَيْنَ عِبَادِكَ فِىْ مَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(46)\nQOLIL AL-LAAHUMMA FAATERA SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE A’AALEMA GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE ANTA TAHKUMU BAYNA E’BAADEKAS FEE MAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “O’ God! the Originator of the heavens and the earth, the Knower of the unseen and the manifest! Thou (alone) shalt judge between Thy servants in the matter wherein they were differing.\nوَلَوْ اَنَّ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مَا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا وَّمِثْلَهٗ مَعَهٗ لَافْتَدَوْا بِهٖ مِنْ سُوْٓءِ الْعَذَابِ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ‌ؕ وَبَدَا لَهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ مَا لَمْ يَكُوْنُوْا يَحْتَسِبُوْنَ‏(47)\nWA LAW ANNAL LILLAZEENA ZALAMOO MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A WWAMESLAH MA-A’HU LAAFTADAWA BEHI MIN SOOE A’ZAABE YAWMA AL-QEEMATE WABADAA LAHUM MENAL LAAHE MAA LAM YAKOONOOA YAHTASEBOONA.\nAnd had it been for those who did injustice, whatever is in the earth and the like added to it, they verily will seek to ransom themselves with it from the pain of the chastisement on the Day of Judgment; and there shall appear unto them, from God, that which they had not been reckoning.\nوَبَدَا لَهُمْ سَيِّاٰتُ مَا كَسَبُوْا وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(48)\nWABADAA LAHUM SAYAAATU MAA KASABOO WAHAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nAnd shall appear unto them the evils of what they wrought, and shall surround them that which they used to mock at.\nفَاِذَا مَسَّ الْاِنْسَانَ ضُرٌّ دَعَانَا ثُمَّ اِذَا خَوَّلْنٰهُ نِعْمَةً مِّنَّا ۙ قَالَ اِنَّمَاۤ اُوْتِيْتُهٗ عَلٰى عِلْمٍ‌ؕ بَلْ هِىَ فِتْنَةٌ وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(49)\nFA-EZAA MASSAN INSAANA ZURRUN DAA’AANAA SUMMA EZAA KHAWLNAAHU NEA’MATAN MINNAA QAALA INNAMAA OOTEETOHU A’LAA E’ELMIN BAL HEYA FITNATUN WA LAAKINNA AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd when toucheth man a harm he crieth unto Us; then when We grant him a favour from Us, sayeth he; “I have been granted it only on account of (my) knowledge.” Nay! it is only a trial, but most of them know not.\nقَدْ قَالَهَا الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ فَمَاۤ اَغْنٰى عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(50)\nQAD QAALAHAA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FAMAA AGHNAA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nIndeed, the same did say those before them, but availed them not what they had been earning.\nفَاَصَابَهُمْ سَيِّاٰتُ مَا كَسَبُوْا‌ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مِنْ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ سَيُصِيْبُهُمْ سَيِّاٰتُ مَا كَسَبُوْا ۙ وَمَا هُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ‏(51)\nFAASAABAHUM SAYAAATU MAA KASABOO WAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO MIN HAAOOLAAA-E SAYUSEEBUHUM SAYAAATU MAA KASABOO WA MAA HUM BE-MO’JEZEENA.\nSo befell unto them the evils what they did earn; and (for) those of these who did injustice, soon shall befall unto them the evils what they did earn, and they shall frustrate Us not (in Our Plans).\nاَوَلَمْ يَعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(52)\nAWALAM YAA’LAMOOA ANNAL LAAHA YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA YAQDER INNAL FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nWhat! know they not that (it is) God (alone Who) amplifieth the sustenance unto whomsoever He willeth, and straiteneth (it) (whosoever He willeth); Verily in this are signs for a people who believe.\nقُلْ يٰعِبَادِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَسْرَفُوْا عَلٰٓى اَنْفُسِهِمْ لَا تَقْنَطُوْا مِنْ رَّحْمَةِ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوْبَ جَمِيْعًا‌ ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْغَفُوْرُ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(53)\nQUL YAA E’BAADEYAL LAZEENA AASRAFOOA A’LAA ANFOSEHIM LAA TAQNATOOA MIN RRAHMATE LAAHE INNAL LAAHA YAGHFERO AZ-ZUNOOBA JAMEE-A’A INNAHU HOWA GHAFOORUL RAHEEM.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “O’ My servants! who have been extravagant unto their own selves, despair ye not of the mercy of God; verily God forgiveth sins all together; verily He is the Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nوَاَنِيْبُوْۤا اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ وَاَسْلِمُوْا لَهٗ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّاْتِيَكُمُ الْعَذَابُ ثُمَّ لَا تُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(54)\nWAANEEBOOA ELAA RABBEKUM WAASLEMOOA LAHU MIN QABLE AN YAATEYAKOMUT A’ZAABO SUMMA LAA TUNSAROONA.\nAnd return ye unto your Lord, and resign ye yourselves unto Him, ere cometh unto you the chastisement, for then ye shall not be helped.\nوَاتَّبِعُوْۤا اَحْسَنَ مَاۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّاْتِيَكُمُ الْعَذَابُ بَغْتَةً وَّاَنْتُمْ لَا تَشْعُرُوْنَۙ‏(55)\nWA TABE-O’O AHSANAL MAA UNZELA ELAYKUM MIN RABBEKUM MIN QABLE AN YAATEYAKOMUT A’ZAABO BAGHTATANW WA ANTUL LAA TASH-O’ROON.\nAnd follow ye the most excellent thing what hath been sent down unto you from your Lord, ere cometh unto you the chastisement suddenly while ye even perceive it not,\nاَنْ تَقُوْلَ نَفْسٌ يّٰحَسْرَتٰى عَلٰى مَا فَرَّطْتُّ فِىْ جَنْۢبِ اللّٰهِ وَاِنْ كُنْتُ لَمِنَ السّٰخِرِيْنَۙ‏(56)\nAN TAQOOLA NAFSUN YYAAHASRATAA A’LAA MAA FARRATTTU FEE JANBE LAAHE WA KUNTO LAMENAS AS-SAAKHEREENA.\nLest a soul should say: “Oh! Alas, Woe unto me! for what I failed (in my duty) unto God, and certainly was I of those who mocked,\nاَوْ تَقُوْلَ لَوْ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ هَدٰٮنِىْ لَكُنْتُ مِنَ الْمُتَّقِيْنَۙ‏(57)\nAW TAQOOLA LAW ANNAL LAAHA HADAANEAA LAKUNTU MENAL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nOr, it should say: “Had God guided me, I would certainly have been of the pious ones,\nاَوْ تَقُوْلَ حِيْنَ تَرَى الْعَذَابَ لَوْ اَنَّ لِىْ كَرَّةً فَاَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(58)\nAW TAQOOLA HEENA TARAL A’ZAABA LAW ANNAL LEE KARRATAN FA SHAY-IWN WA MENAL MOHSENEEN.\nOr, it should say when it seeth the chastisement: “Had there been only a return for me, I would be of the righteous (ones)\nبَلٰى قَدْ جَآءَتْكَ اٰيٰتِىْ فَكَذَّبْتَ بِهَا وَاسْتَكْبَرْتَ وَكُنْتَ مِنَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(59)\nBALAA QAD JAAATKA AAAYAATEAA FAKAZZABTA BEHAA WAASTAKBARTA WA KUNTA MENAL KAAFEREEN.\nNay! indeed did come unto thee My signs, then thou didst belie them, thou didst act proudly and thou wert of the disbelievers.\nوَيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ تَرَى الَّذِيْنَ كَذَبُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ وُجُوْهُهُمْ مُّسْوَدَّةٌ ؕ اَلَيْسَ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ مَثْوًى لِّلْمُتَكَبِّرِيْنَ‏(60)\nWA YAWMA QEYAAMATE TARAL LAZEENA KAZABOOA A’LAL LAAHE WOJOOHOHUM MMUSWADDATUN A-LAYSA FEE JAHANNAMA MASWAL LLELMUTAKABBEREENA.\nAnd on the Day of Resurrection thou shalt see those who have uttered lies against God their faces shall be blackened; is there not in Hell an abode for the proud?\nوَيُنَجِّىْ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا بِمَفَازَتِهِمْ لَا يَمَسُّهُمُ السُّوْٓءُ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُوْنَ‏(61)\nWAYUNAJJEAA LAAHO LAZEENA TAQAW BEMAFAAZATEHEM LAA YAMASSUHUMU AS-SOOU WA LAA HUM HUM YAHZANOON.\nAnd shall deliver God those who guard (themselves) against evil, with their success: evil shall touch them not, nor shall they grieve.\nاَللّٰهُ خَالِقُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ‌ وَّ هُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّكِيْلٌ‏(62)\nALLAAHO KHAALEQU KULLE SHAY-IN WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WWAKEELUN.\nGod (alone) is the Creator of everything, and He (alone) is over all things the Guardian.\nلَّهٗ مَقَالِيْدُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(63)\nLAHU MAQAALEEDU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WA LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nHis are the keys of the heavens and the earth; and those who disbelieve in the signs of God, these are they who are the losers.\nقُلْ اَفَغَيْرَ اللّٰهِ تَاْمُرُوْٓنِّىْۤ اَعْبُدُ اَيُّهَا الْجٰهِلُوْنَ‏(64)\nQUL AAFAGHAYRA LAAHE TAAMUROONNEAA A-A’BODUL AYYOHAL AL-JAAHELOONA.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!)'. “What! Bid ye me to worship others than God? O’ ye ignorant ones!\nوَلَقَدْ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْكَ وَاِلَى الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِكَ‌ۚ لَئِنْ اَشْرَكْتَ لَيَحْبَطَنَّ عَمَلُكَ وَلَتَكُوْنَنَّ مِنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(65)\nWA LAQAD OOHEYA ELAYKA WA ELAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEKA LAIL AASHRAKTA LAYAHBATANNA A’AMALUKA WALATAKOONANNA MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nAnd indeed hath it been revealed unto thee and unto those before thee: “Verily if thou associatest (others with God), certainly would come to naught thy work, and certainly wouldst thou be of the losers.\nبَلِ اللّٰهَ فَاعْبُدْ وَكُنْ مِّنَ الشّٰكِرِيْنَ‏(66)\nBALIL LAAHA FAAA’BUD WA KUN MENAL ASH-SHAAKEREENA.\nNay! But God alone, worship thou and be of the thankful ones.\nوَمَا قَدَرُوْا اللّٰهَ حَقَّ قَدْرِهٖ ‌ۖ  وَالْاَرْضُ جَمِيْعًا قَبْضَتُهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وَالسَّمٰوٰتُ مَطْوِيّٰتٌۢ بِيَمِيْنِهٖ‌ ؕ سُبْحٰنَهٗ وَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(67)\nWA MAA QADAROOA LAAHA HAQQA QADREH WAL JAMEE-A’A QABZATUH YAWMA QEYAAMATE WAALSSAMAAWAATU MATWEETUN BE-YAMEENEHI WALADAN TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nThey have esteemed not God, as it is His rightful due; While the whole earth shall be in His grip on the Day of Judgment and heavens rolled up (shall be) in His right hand; Hallowed is He, high above what they associate (with Him).\nوَنُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ فَصَعِقَ مَنْ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا مَنْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ‌ ؕ ثُمَّ نُفِخَ فِيْهِ اُخْرٰى فَاِذَا هُمْ قِيَامٌ يَّنْظُرُوْنَ‏(68)\nWA FIL SOORE FASAE’EQA MAN FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAN FIL ARZE ILLAA MAN SHAAA-AL LAAHO SUMMA NUFEKHA FEEHE LAHU FA-EZAA HUM QEEAMUN YYANZUROONA.\nAnd (when) shall be blown the Trumpet, then shall swoon (die) whoever is in the heavens and whoever is in the earth save those whom God hath willed (to keep alive); then (the Trumpet) shall be blown again, then lo! they shall stand up awaiting.\nوَاَشْرَقَتِ الْاَرْضُ بِنُوْرِ رَبِّهَا وَوُضِعَ الْكِتٰبُ وَجِآىْ ئَ بِالنَّبِيّٖنَ وَالشُّهَدَآءِ وَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(69)\nWAASHRAQATE ARZO BENOORE RABBEHAA WAWUZEA’A KETAABO WAJEAAAAA A BE-NABIYYEENA WA AN WA BAYNAHUM BIL-HAQQE WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nAnd the earth shall get radiant with the light of its Lord, and the Book (of deeds) shall be set, and the prophets shall be brought up and the witnesses, and (it shall) be judged between them, and they shall not be dealt with unjustly.\nوَوُفِّيَتْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّا عَمِلَتْ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَفْعَلُوْنَ‏(70)\nWAWUFFEET KULLO NAFSIM MAA A’MELAT WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BEMAA YAF-A’LOON.\nAnd shall be paid in full unto every soul what it hath wrought, and He knoweth best what they do.\nوَسِيْقَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِلٰى جَهَنَّمَ زُمَرًا‌ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءُوْهَا فُتِحَتْ اَبْوَابُهَا وَقَالَ لَهُمْ خَزَنَتُهَاۤ اَلَمْ يَاْتِكُمْ رُسُلٌ مِّنْكُمْ يَتْلُوْنَ عَلَيْكُمْ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّكُمْ وَيُنْذِرُوْنَكُمْ لِقَآءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هٰذَا‌ ؕ قَالُوْا بَلٰى وَلٰكِنْ حَقَّتْ كَلِمَةُ الْعَذَابِ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(71)\nWASEEQA LAZEENA KAFAROO ELAA JAHANNAMA ZUMARAN HATTAA EZAA JAAA-OOHAA FUTEHAT AABWAABUHAA WA QAALA LAHUM KHAZANATOHAA ALAM YAATEKUM RUSULUN MINKUM YATLOONAL A’LAYKUM AAYAATIL RABBEKUM WAYUNZEROONAKUM LE-QAAA-AL YAWMEKUM HAAZAA QAALOO BALAA WA LAAKIL HAQQAT KALEMATU A’ZAABE A’LAL KAAFEREEN.\nAnd shall be driven those who disbelieved, unto the Hell, in flocks; Until, when come they to it, its doors shall be opened and shall say unto them the keepers of it; “Came not unto you apostles from among you reciting unto you the signs of your Lord and warning you of the meeting of this your day?” they shall say; “Yea! but just is the sentence of punishment on the disbelievers\nقِيْلَ ادْخُلُوْۤا اَبْوَابَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ۚ فَبِئْسَ مَثْوَى الْمُتَكَبِّرِيْنَ‏(72)\nQEELA KHOLOO AABWAABA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA FA MASALUL MASWAA AL-MUTAKABBEREENA.\nIt shall be said (unto them): “Enter ye (Now) the gates of Hell, to abide therein, and wretched the abode of the arrogant.\nوَسِيْقَ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّقَوْا رَبَّهُمْ اِلَى الْجَنَّةِ زُمَرًا‌ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءُوْهَا وَفُتِحَتْ اَبْوَابُهَا وَقَالَ لَهُمْ خَزَنَتُهَا سَلٰمٌ عَلَيْكُمْ طِبْتُمْ فَادْخُلُوْهَا خٰلِدِيْنَ‏(73)\nWASEEQA LAZEENA TAQAW RABBAHUM ELAL JANNAH ZUMARAN HATTAA EZAA JAAA-OOHAA WAFUTEHAT AABWAABUHAA WA QAALA LAHUM KHAZANATOHAA SALAAMUN A’LAYKUM TEBTUM FAADKHULOOHAA KHAALEDEENA.\nAnd shall be conveyed those who feared (the wrath of) their Lord, in companies unto the garden; until when they come to it, and its doors shall be opened, and the keepers of it shall say unto them: “Peace be on you! ye shall be happy; Enter it then to abide.\nوَقَالُوا الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ صَدَقَنَا وَعْدَهٗ وَاَوْرَثَنَا الْاَرْضَ نَتَبَوَّاُ مِنَ الْجَنَّةِ حَيْثُ نَشَآءُ ‌ۚ فَنِعْمَ اَجْرُ الْعٰمِلِيْنَ‏(74)\nWA HAMDO LILLAAHE LAZEE SADAQANAA WA’DAHU WAAWRASANAA ARZA NATABAWAU MENAL JANNAH HAYSO NASHAAA-O FA NE’MA AJRUL A’AMELEENAL.\nAnd they shall say: “All praise is God’s, Who hath made good to us His promise, and He hath made us to inherit the earth, we may dwell in the gardens wherever we please, and goodly is the recompense of the workers (of good deeds).\nوَتَرَى الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ حَآفِّيْنَ مِنْ حَوْلِ الْعَرْشِ يُسَبِّحُوْنَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ‌ۚ وَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَقِيْلَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(75)\nWA TARAL AL-MALAAAEKATA HAAFFEENA MIN HAWLE A’RSHIL YUSABBEHOONA BE-HAMDE RABBEHIM WA BAYNAHUM BIL-HAQQE WA QEELAD HAMDO LILLAAHE RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd thou shalt see the angels circling around the ‘Arsh’ (The Throne of Absolute Authority), celebrating the Praise of their Lord; and it shall be judged between them with justice, and it shall be said, All praise is God’s the Lord of the worlds!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Zumar (The Companies)\nThis Surah has 75 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said that whoever recites this Surah will be given a honourable and respectable status in this life and in the hereafter. Allah (s.w.t.) will give him so much respect in the eyes of the people that they will be in awe. The fire of Jahannam will be made haraam on his body (ie. he will never enter hell fire) and the gifts he will get in Jannah will be countless.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that is a person keeps this Surah (written) in his possession then whoever meets him will praise him. If this Surah is tied to one’s arm then whoever sees him will praise him."
}
